# Allocations memcheck reaches through this tree but which this tree
# does not own. The same two libraries are named to LeakSanitizer in
# tests/lsan.supp, for the same reason.
#
# The font configuration library builds a process-wide cache the first
# time a font is asked for and holds it until the process ends, by its
# own design; the XML parser it reads its configuration files with is
# reached only from there. Neither allocation belongs to a context, so
# neither is freed when one ends, and neither grows with the work a
# process does. They are named here so that the leaks the tree does own
# are what the job reports.
{
   the font configuration library's process-wide cache
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible
   ...
   obj:*/libfontconfig.so*
}
{
   the XML parser that library reads its configuration with
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible
   ...
   obj:*/libexpat.so*
}

# The shell each script-driven test is run by. meson applies the wrapper
# to the whole test command, and most of this suite's tests are a shell
# script that starts the interpreter, so the process memcheck watches is
# the shell. What it holds when it exits is the shell's own and is named
# here; the interpreter it started is a child, and memcheck does not
# follow one by default.
{
   the shell a test is run by, not the tree
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible
   ...
   obj:*/dash
}
{
   the shell a test is run by, not the tree (bash)
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect,possible
   ...
   obj:*/bash
}
